{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00012",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.3,
      "end_seconds": 3.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Hi. Thanks for coming in today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.31,
      "end_seconds": 5.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "Good afternoon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.05,
      "end_seconds": 10.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "tell me from the beginning, what's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.4,
      "end_seconds": 17.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.94,
      "text": "It's dark urine. I thought I'd wait, but it it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.57,
      "end_seconds": 21.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "How long has this been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.33,
      "end_seconds": 33.64,
      "duration_seconds": 10.31,
      "text": "Right, hm. It was either the end of last month or earlier than that. I couldn't tell you the date."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.71,
      "end_seconds": 42.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "And what do you do to cope with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.6,
      "end_seconds": 47.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "It settles a little with drinking more water."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.58,
      "end_seconds": 51.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "have you been feeling dizzy when you stand?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.62,
      "end_seconds": 71.72,
      "duration_seconds": 19.1,
      "text": "Yeah. Five days, I'd say. As for feeling dizzy when I stand, it feels severe to me. It sort of comes and goes. I get some relief from sitting down. Oh, and muscle cramps. That's been about the same, ten days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.1,
      "end_seconds": 73.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Okay, keep going."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.19,
      "end_seconds": 75.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "And diarrhoea, too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.73,
      "end_seconds": 85.71,
      "duration_seconds": 7.98,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.48,
      "end_seconds": 95.1,
      "duration_seconds": 8.62,
      "text": "So, I'd say every other day. Maybe a four out of ten on a bad day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 103.83,
      "end_seconds": 120.18,
      "duration_seconds": 16.35,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Pressure 103 over 60, BMI works out to 18.2, height 186 centimetres, weight 63 kilos, SpO2 99 percent on room air, heart rate 102, temp 37.2 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.26,
      "end_seconds": 122.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.07,
      "text": "okay, noted"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.6,
      "end_seconds": 127.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.33,
      "end_seconds": 133.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "a little pressure here, tell me if it's tender"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.37,
      "end_seconds": 156.73,
      "duration_seconds": 7.36,
      "text": "your mouth is quite dry and the skin is a little slow to spring back"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.43,
      "end_seconds": 163.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "That's fine, sit up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.65,
      "end_seconds": 182.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Have you noticed blood in the stool or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.27,
      "end_seconds": 185.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Nothing like that, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.98,
      "end_seconds": 189.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Okay, and what about fainting or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.66,
      "end_seconds": 193.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "No, no fainting or fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.87,
      "end_seconds": 197.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.07,
      "end_seconds": 199.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "No rashes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.94,
      "end_seconds": 202.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.85,
      "end_seconds": 207.91,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "Hmm, you know, no, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.84,
      "end_seconds": 212.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.2,
      "end_seconds": 218.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "I've had diabetes for about ten years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.76,
      "end_seconds": 220.6,
      "duration_seconds": 0.84,
      "text": "I follow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.19,
      "end_seconds": 226.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "I've had high blood pressure, yes. I've had gout, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.05,
      "end_seconds": 234.92,
      "duration_seconds": 7.87,
      "text": "Right, so diabetes is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Anything special about your diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.05,
      "end_seconds": 239.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "I try to avoid too much sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.24,
      "end_seconds": 243.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Do you have a job?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.56,
      "end_seconds": 246.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "I'm a self-employed electrician."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.47,
      "end_seconds": 251.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.84,
      "end_seconds": 281.29,
      "duration_seconds": 28.45,
      "text": "Yeah, I'm on glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast for my sugar. It's the not knowing that gets to me. A A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it. Um, I take ramipril, 5 milligrams, every morning for my blood pressure. Allopurinol, 100 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 282.5,
      "end_seconds": 287.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 50 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.0,
      "end_seconds": 293.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Right. Do you happen to have the current prescription here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 294.45,
      "end_seconds": 298.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "not with me. I'll bring it next time"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.03,
      "end_seconds": 304.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.67,
      "end_seconds": 318.01,
      "duration_seconds": 12.34,
      "text": "hmm, there was some antibiotic, I was told I was allergic. But I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.44,
      "end_seconds": 339.91,
      "duration_seconds": 9.47,
      "text": "so, based on the history and the examination, I'd lean towards dehydration from a stomach bug. An electrolyte imbalance is still possible"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 341.95,
      "end_seconds": 347.9,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "I've, I've been thinking the worst, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.45,
      "end_seconds": 365.7,
      "duration_seconds": 17.25,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now dehydration from a stomach bug is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let's get blood salts, for dehydration. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.0,
      "end_seconds": 369.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "okay, you know, that's fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 371.43,
      "end_seconds": 403.53,
      "duration_seconds": 32.1,
      "text": "let's book a kidney function test to look into dehydration. I'll start you on ORS, 1 sachet, after each loose motion, for two days. That's for dehydration. Small, frequent sips are better than a big glass at once, and keep going even if you don't feel thirsty. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. Let's review you in three days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 404.87,
      "end_seconds": 406.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Sure, that's doable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 408.22,
      "end_seconds": 411.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "That's it on my side. Anything unclear?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 413.24,
      "end_seconds": 416.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Okay, you know, thank you. Bye."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 417.15,
      "end_seconds": 418.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "bye for now"
    }
  ]
}